wait for my applause."

00:02:35.788 --> 00:02:37.323 size:75% position:38%
Like, those moments,
those canned moments

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:39.159 align:start size:94% position:6%
never, ever, ever, ever work
-Yeah.

00:02:39.159 --> 00:02:42.195 size:75% position:38%
-But I can't imagine
that they're not all
going to plan one.

00:02:42.195 --> 00:02:46.266
-It does seem like audiences
now, or I should say voters now,

00:02:46.266 --> 00:02:48.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
have a better sense
for authenticity.

00:02:48.268 --> 00:02:50.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
And one thing you have to sa
about Donald Trump,

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:53.840
he is authentically himsel
and was at every debate.

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:55.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, there was never a time
where he was like,

00:02:55.608 --> 00:02:57.577 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, I have to get
to my preplanned line."

00:02:57.577 --> 00:03:00.380 align:start size:94% position:6%
They were just like -- I don't
think he preplans anything

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:02.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Got to make sure
I get the details

00:03:02.315 --> 00:03:03.082 line:92%
of this policy just right.

00:03:03.082 --> 00:03:05.318 align:start size:94% position:6%
That didn't happen.
-I think inside, he's like

00:03:05.318 --> 00:03:07.220 align:start size:94% position:6%
