just want to lie low

00:05:42.542 --> 00:05:45.378
and hopefully nobody notices you
and you can keep riding

00:05:45.378 --> 00:05:46.112 size:81% position:41% line:92%
your name recognition?

00:05:46.112 --> 00:05:48.981 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I feel like Bernie
is very bad at that.

00:05:48.981 --> 00:05:51.684 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ] Lying low?
-Yeah, lying low.

00:05:51.684 --> 00:05:55.388 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I'm just going to stand her
and not be noticed!!"

00:05:55.388 --> 00:05:57.957
I want to talk real quick --
Before we go to commercial

00:05:57.957 --> 00:06:00.426 align:start size:94% position:6%
I want to talk about this idea
about electability.

00:06:00.426 --> 00:06:02.061 align:start size:94% position:6%
Everybody's talking
about electability.

00:06:02.061 --> 00:06:05.298
And I think when you go back
to our last two presidents

00:06:05.298 --> 00:06:07.600 align:start size:94% position:6%
neither of them
seemed at all electable

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:10.636 align:start size:94% position:6%
until they were president.
-Yeah.

00:06:10.636 --> 00:06:11.671 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-You know, I mean --

00:06:11.671 --> 00:06:13.639 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Even in retrospect,
they don't seem like it.

00:06:13.639 --> 00:06:16.376
-You know, but there was -- Yo
know, we obviously never elected

00:06:16.376 --> 00:06:18.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
a black man president unti
President Barack Obama,

00:06:18.444 --> 00:06:21.714
and we never elected whateve
it is that Donald Trump is

00:06:21.714 --> 00:06:24.150 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's the first of it.
He's the first of his kind

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:26.552 align:start size:94% position:6%
So what -- Do you think people
are too caught up in it,

00:06:26.552 --> 00:06:29.455 align:start size:94% position:6%
or do you think it is just
this sort of core fear

00:06:29.455 --> 00:06:31.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
of the Democratic Party
right now

00:06:31.424 --> 00:06:32.458 line:92%
not to have the same outcome

00:06:32.458 --> 00:06:35.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think it's both
totally understandable

00:06:35.661 --> 00:06:36.396 line:92%
and also a fool's errand.

00:06:36.396 --> 00:06:39.999
I mean, I think that Democrats
looking at their field right now

00:06:39.999 --> 00:06:42.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
probably see a lot
that they like in that field

00:06:42.268 --> 00:06:44.637 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, if there's something
that you don't like

00:06:44.637 --> 00:06:45.505 line:92%
about one of the candidates,

00:06:45.505 --> 00:06:46.472 align:start size:94% position:6%
there's 22 others
to choose from.

00:06:46.472 --> 00:06:48.841 align:start size:94% position:6%
And there's plenty --
There's plenty there on offer.

00:06:48.841 --> 00:06:52.311
I think the unifying thing
that does motivate all Democrats

00:06:52.311 --> 00:06:54.180 align:start size:94% position:6%
and a lot of independents
right now

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:55.982 align:start size:94% position:6%
is the desire to get Trump
out of there.

00:06:55.982 --> 00:06:58.618 size:84% position:42%
That's just going to be
the dominating factor

00:06:58.618 --> 00:06:59.452 size:75% position:38% line:92%
in a field this big.

00:06:59.452 --> 00:07:03.790
It's really, therefore, hard not
to approach the primary proces

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:05.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
as something
you ought to game out

00:07:05.958 --> 00:07:07.427 align:start size:94% position:6%
in terms of who's
most electable.

00:07:07.427 --> 00:07:10.062 align:start size:94% position:6%
The problem with that
is that nobody can tell,

00:07:10.062 --> 00:07:12.498 align:start size:94% position:6%
and when you try to make
your voting decision

00:07:12.498 --> 00:07:15.968
based on not who you think
is your favorite candidate

00:07:15.968 --> 00:07:17.236 line:92%
but who you think everybody else

00:07:17.236 --> 00:07:19.705 size:75% position:38%
might think is their
favorite candidate,

00:07:19.705 --> 00:07:20.807 line:92%
it's just dumb game theory

00:07:20.807 --> 00:07:22.308 align:start size:94% position:6%
It just doesn't work
mathematically.

00:07:22.308 --> 00:07:25.311
The best thing you can do fo
your country in the primar

00:07:25.311 --> 00:07:28.481 size:78% position:39%
is, A, pay attention,
B, commit to vote,

00:07:28.481 --> 00:07:29.649 line:92%
and, C, vote for the perso

00:07:29.649 --> 00:07:31.484 size:75% position:38%
you think would make
the best president.

00:07:31.484 --> 00:07:33.486 align:start size:94% position:6%
Any other way
you try to outthink it,

00:07:33.486 --> 00:07:35.822 align:start size:94% position:6%
you're going to undo
the point of the process.

00:07:35.822 --> 00:07:39.692
-Well, I hope we get a ste
closer after the debates.

